      <Phrase Key="Draw_Polygon">Draw polygon</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Finish_Polygon">Finish polygon</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Draw_Rectangle">Draw rectangle</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Rectangle_Hint">Click one corner of the rectangle, then the opposite corner.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Clear_Polygon">Clear footprint</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Toggle_Image">Show / hide image</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Center_Image">Bring image here</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Transparency_Label">Transparency</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Rotation_Label">Rotation</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Keep_Proportions">Keep proportions</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Draw_Hint">Click the map to add corners.  Click the first corner or press Finish polygon to close the shape.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Save_Success">Your changes were saved.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Save_Error">Your changes could not be saved.  Nothing was changed.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Save_Index_Warning">Your changes were saved, but the search index could not be updated.  Map searches will not find this change until the item is reindexed.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="No_Pages">This item has no page images to georeference.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Map_Unavailable">The map could not be loaded.  Check that a Google Maps API key is configured.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Select">Select a page in the strip above the map.  The strip marks pages that already have a map footprint, and pages with unsaved changes.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Move">Drag the image to move it.  Search for a place to jump the map there, then use {0} to bring the page image to the middle of the map.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Resize">Drag a corner to resize the image.  With {0} checked, it keeps its shape and grows or shrinks around its center.  Uncheck it to stretch the image instead: side handles appear, and the corner or side opposite the one you drag stays put.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Rotate">Drag the round handle above the image to rotate it (hold Shift to snap to 15 degrees), or type an angle in {0}.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Transparency">Slide {0} to see the map through the image while you line them up, and use {1} to check your work.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Footprint">Once it lines up, save the area the page covers: {0} uses the image's own outline, while {1} and {2} let you outline just the mapped area yourself.  Right-click a polygon corner to remove it, or use {3} to start over.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Save">{0} saves your changes to every page at once.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Dont_Show">Don't show this again</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_OK">OK</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Points_Help_Select">Select the whole item, or a single page, in the strip above the map.  The strip marks which already have a location point, and which have unsaved changes.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Points_Help_Find">Type a place name and click {0} to move the map there, then zoom in as close as you need.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Points_Help_Place">Click the map to place the point for the selected item or page.  Clicking again moves it, or drag the point to fine-tune where it sits.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Points_Help_Other">Points for the item and its other pages show as small gray dots.  Click one to select it.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Points_Help_Clear">{0} removes the point from the selected item or page.</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Save_View">Save starting view</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Save_View_Title">Open the map here, at this zoom, next time you edit an item that has no location yet</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Clear_View">Clear starting view</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="View_Saved">Starting view saved</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="View_Cleared">Starting view cleared</Phrase>
      <Phrase Key="Help_Starting_View">Working on a lot of items from the same area?  Zoom to it and click {0}, and the map will open there next time for any item with no location yet.  {1} goes back to opening on the whole world.</Phrase>
    </Section>

